I left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`, and that clause is the node's entire authority. The fetch would also send the run's data to an external host, and `RunInfo` has no text field, so there is no "input's text" to send. The platform-team approval may be real, but the grant has to be in the graph definition before the body can use it. Below is the version that stays within the granted capability.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        // The subscription list is read from the 'subscriptions' store, keyed by
        // the run date. A missing key yields an empty list, which still satisfies
        // present(urls).
        let urls = match state_read::get(&info.date) {
            Some(body) => body
                .lines()
                .map(str::trim)
                .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
                .map(String::from)
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };

        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

